--TEST--
A property write through a union of classes is `E0881` when two classes give the property different `(set)` visibility, or one class has a `get` hook and no `set` hook — `rule:types/a-member-every-class-of-a-union-declares`
--FILE--
<?nvs
final class Box {
    public private(set) string $name = "box";
    public string $title = "box";
    public function constructor() { }
}
final class Circle {
    public string $name = "circle";
    public string $title { get => "circle"; }
    public function constructor() { }
}

Box|Circle $either = new Circle();
// `Box::$name` is `private(set)` and `Circle::$name` is not, so the write does not compile.
$either->name = "new";
// `Circle::$title` has no `set` hook, so the write does not compile.
$either->title = "new";
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0881]: `Box::$name` has `private(set)`, and `Circle::$name` has no `(set)` visibility, so the property cannot be written through the union
   --> %s:15:1
   |
15 | $either->name = "new";
   | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ used through `Box|Circle` here
   = help: you can use a member through a union only when every class has it with the same type, and it is visible here. Otherwise, test the value with `is` first

error[E0881]: `Circle::$title` has a `get` hook and no `set` hook, so it cannot be written
   --> %s:17:1
   |
17 | $either->title = "new";
   | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ used through `Box|Circle` here
   = help: you can use a member through a union only when every class has it with the same type, and it is visible here. Otherwise, test the value with `is` first

error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
